// Red fire doors with panic bars, facing <side>. true: the real exit (runexit). fake: a fake exit (runfake); fake-open: it swung inward onto an empty closet. marked: the door you came in by, a huge red '!' on its inside (runmarked). entry: the way in, set into a wall in Levels 1 and 37 (runentry). arrival: the door left where an escaped runner comes out, flush on a wall in the air block in front of it, a NO RE-ENTRY placard on its face (runentry). returned: that door set into a wall like entry, replacing an ordinary door in Levels 1, 4 and The End once a runner has escaped; red, no EXIT, a NO RE-ENTRY placard on both faces (runentry). The true and fake doors' lower halves stop short of the floor; the true one shows a faint daylight in the gap and gives off a soft light, the fake one only dark
